    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "pantry-bot — Twitch bot; no app metrics, readiness is the only 'is it healthy' signal",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 53 },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "About HTTP health here",
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 54 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "pantry-bot has **no `/health` or `/healthz` endpoint** -- `GET /` returns a bare 404 (verified through the live tunnel). The k8s probes are `exec` checks (`node -e \"require('http').get(...)\"`) reproducing the old Compose healthcheck's \"any response, even a 404, proves the server is alive\" logic, specifically *because* an `httpGet` probe would treat that same 404 as a failure and crash-loop a healthy pod. That means there is no Prometheus series for HTTP health -- the panels below (readiness, restarts) are the only signal Kubernetes can give us, sourced from the exec probe's pass/fail via kube-state-metrics. **TODO for real HTTP health visibility:** add `app.get('/healthz', (_req, res) => res.status(200).send('ok'))` to the bot (noted as the preferred fix in `pantry-bot/40-deployment.yaml`), switch the probes to `httpGet`, and this dashboard could then plot actual request latency/status if the route is later instrumented with `prom-client`. Until then, do not invent a metric name for this."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Readiness (proxy for HTTP health)",
      "description": "kube_pod_status_ready, condition=true. This reflects the exec probe passing, which only proves the Node HTTP server on :3000 accepted a TCP connection and returned any response -- not that Twitch auth, the SQLite DB, or the Cloudflare tunnel are functioning.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 58 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" },
      "targets": [{ "refId": "A", "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" }, "expr": "min(kube_pod_status_ready{namespace=\"pantry-bot\", condition=\"true\"})", "legendFormat": "ready" }],
      "options": { "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false }, "orientation": "auto", "textMode": "auto", "colorMode": "background", "graphMode": "none", "justifyMode": "auto" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "mappings": [
            { "type": "value", "options": { "0": { "text": "NOT READY", "color": "red", "index": 0 } } },
            { "type": "value", "options": { "1": { "text": "READY", "color": "green", "index": 1 } } }
          ],
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "red", "value": null }, { "color": "green", "value": 1 }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Restarts (24h)",
      "description": "livenessProbe failureThreshold is 5 (150s of continuous failure) specifically because a restart here means real downtime -- strategy: Recreate + a single RWO SQLite PVC means the old pod fully terminates before the new one mounts. Frequent restarts are worth chasing down, not shrugging off.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 6, "x": 6, "y": 58 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" },
      "targets": [{ "refId": "A", "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" }, "expr": "sum(increase(kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total{namespace=\"pantry-bot\", container=\"bot\"}[24h])) or vector(0)", "legendFormat": "restarts" }],
      "options": { "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false }, "orientation": "auto", "textMode": "auto", "colorMode": "background", "graphMode": "none", "justifyMode": "auto" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "green", "value": null }, { "color": "#EAB839", "value": 1 }, { "color": "red", "value": 2 }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "gauge",
      "title": "bot Memory vs 256Mi Limit",
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 6, "x": 12, "y": 58 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" },
      "targets": [{ "refId": "A", "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" }, "expr": "sum(container_memory_working_set_bytes{namespace=\"pantry-bot\", container=\"bot\"})" }],
      "options": { "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false }, "showThresholdLabels": false, "showThresholdMarkers": true },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 268435456,
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "green", "value": null }, { "color": "#EAB839", "value": 201326592 }, { "color": "red", "value": 228065280 }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "cloudflared Sidecar Up",
      "description": "The Cloudflare tunnel container in the same pod. If pantry-bot itself is Ready but this container has restarted, the Twitch bot may be running with no public ingress at all.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 6, "x": 18, "y": 58 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" },
      "targets": [{ "refId": "A", "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}" }, "expr": "min(kube_pod_container_status_running{namespace=\"pantry-bot\", container=\"cloudflared\"})", "legendFormat": "running" }],
      "options": { "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false }, "orientation": "auto", "textMode": "auto", "colorMode": "background", "graphMode": "none", "justifyMode": "auto" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "mappings": [
            { "type": "value", "options": { "0": { "text": "DOWN", "color": "red", "index": 0 } } },
            { "type": "value", "options": { "1": { "text": "UP", "color": "green", "index": 1 } } }
          ],
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "red", "value": null }, { "color": "green", "value": 1 }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
